                  <section ID="LINK_56f4e334-b0a9-463f-abee-d69685ef369a">
                     <id root="74df274e-35df-4757-8429-e8b8cfbdffd7"/>
                     <code code="42229-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="SPL UNCLASSIFIED SECTION"/>
                     <title>Removal</title>
                     <text>
                        <list listType="unordered" styleCode="Disk">
                           <item>
                              <paragraph>Removal:</paragraph>
                              <paragraph>1. Remove EAZI-BREED CIDR Sheep Inserts by pulling, gently but firmly, on the protruding nylon tail.</paragraph>
                              <paragraph>2. EAZI-BREED CIDR Sheep Inserts may reverse direction within the vagina; therefore, if the nylon tail of the insert is not visible on the day of removal, check the vagina to determine if an insert is present.</paragraph>
                              <paragraph>3. Used (removed) EAZI-BREED CIDR Sheep Inserts must be stored in a sealable container until disposed. Sealed bag/container with used EAZI-BREED CIDR Sheep Inserts must be properly disposed in accordance with applicable local, state and Federal regulations.</paragraph>
                           </item>
                        </list>
                     </text>
                     <effectiveTime value="20160705"/>
                  </section>
